==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|k|a}}

===Etymology===
An old {{etyl|bat|fi}} loan; derived from the same word from which e.g. Lithuanian {{m|lt|gaũras}} is descended. Cognates include Veps and Estonian {{m|et|karv}} and Livonian {{m|liv|kōra}}. Originally ''karva'' only had the meaning "color". In its current meaning it is first mentioned in a biblical text in 1621.<ref>{{R:Hakkinen 2004}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈkɑrʋɑ]|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|kar|va|lang=fi}}
* {{rhymes|ɑ|lang=fi}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|lang=fi}}
{{fi-noun}}

# [[hair]] {{gloss|single hair on human or animal; not used of human head hair except in technical sense}}
# [[fur]]
# {{lb|fi|idiomatic}} [[colors]], [[stripes]]
#: ''näyttää todellinen '''karva'''nsa
#:: to [[show one's true colors|show one's true '''colors''']]
#:: to [[show one's true stripes|show one's true '''stripes''']] {{gloss|to reveal how one really is}}

